      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T21:36:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For this particular one it seems like we only care whether it calls force_shutdown then, since a different test verifies the behavior of force_shutdown with regard to manipulating the signals.\n\nIn this test I am ensuring G3 entry function is called, since this calls `force_shutdown` I used this as my mechanism for ensuring this flow.\n\nBy providing AP Power sequence emulator I am ensuring the board specific code is bound to be called when moving into corresponding power state. \n\n\u003e What I\u0027ve done in https://crrev.com/c/4800415/8 seems like a useful pattern for this, in that the test can mock out the board callbacks when they\u0027re unimportant while still being able to call the real implementation to test it.\n\nWith `AP_PWRSEQ_DRIVER` every `board_ap_power_action_xxxx` function will not available (see CL:4079731). However, we can rely on AP Power sequence emulator to test all board functions by using driver API\u0027s to change power state and fit test requirements.",
      "parentUuid": "0390c050_ed13500b",
      "revId": "a0d0ecb052df4ccf261b70932adcdce1cd70b48d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
